<% content_for :title, "Seller terms · VIVUM Plants" %>

<header class="grid gap-1">
  <p class="vv-kicker">Version <%= @purpose.version %> · Draft</p>
  <h1>Seller terms</h1>
</header>

<p>
  These terms apply to you when you own a seller business on VIVUM Plants, in
  addition to the <%= link_to "terms of use", legal_terms_path %>. They include
  an operator agreement for the buyer information you keep in VIVUM.
</p>

<h2>Your business on VIVUM</h2>

<ul>
  <li>During the pilot, seller access is by invitation only.</li>

  <li>
    You're responsible for your business, the plants you sell, the prices you
    set, and complying with consumer, tax and plant import or permit rules.
  </li>

  <li>
    You decide who joins your business and what role they have. You're
    responsible for what your team does in it.
  </li>

  <li>
    Sales are between you and your buyers. Buyer payments go to your own payment
    provider, not to VIVUM.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Subscriptions</h2>

<p>
  Pilot sellers use VIVUM free during the pilot. Before any paid plan applies,
  we'll tell you the price and what it includes, and you choose whether to
  continue. Existing prices stay until we've given you notice of a change.
</p>

<h2>Your buyers' information: operator agreement</h2>

<p>
  For the buyer information you record in VIVUM (names, contact details, orders,
  messages), you are the responsible party under POPIA and VIVUM Labs acts as
  your operator. That means we:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>
    process buyer information only to provide VIVUM's features to you, and on
    your instructions;
  </li>

  <li>
    keep it confidential and don't use it for our own marketing or sell it;
  </li>

  <li>
    protect it with appropriate security measures, and tell you without undue
    delay if we believe it has been accessed without authorisation;
  </li>

  <li>
    use other providers (such as hosting, email, WhatsApp and AI providers) only
    where needed to run those features, under similar obligations;
  </li>

  <li>
    help you respond to buyers who ask to see, correct or delete their
    information;
  </li>

  <li>
    delete or return buyer information when you close your business account,
    unless the law requires us to keep it.
  </li>
</ul>

<p>
  You confirm that you have a lawful reason to collect and share your buyers'
  information with VIVUM, and that you'll tell your buyers how you use it.
</p>

<h2>Suspension and closing</h2>

<p>
  You can close your business account at any time and export your records first.
  We may suspend a business that breaks these terms or puts buyers at risk, and
  we'll tell you why unless the law prevents it.
</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>

<p>
  When these terms change, owners are asked to accept the new version before
  continuing. South African law applies.
</p>
